--- a/broker/grants/ASSUMPTIONS.md
+++ b/broker/grants/ASSUMPTIONS.md
@@ -37,3 +37,4 @@ a later package, that a reviewer may want to change.
 | GR23 | **Recall rollbacks (recalltool W10).** `meta.recall.rollback` is admitted only from origin `broker:recall` with executor `recall`, and always asks the owner: a low-tier text, verb "forget", with the line recall wrote from broker-known facts (the deleted item's kind, the agent, its restore point, how many actions it carried out since). It runs only on the owner's YES; NO or a lapse closes it, the owner's NO with the reason "not approved: owner", which recall tells from no answer. Guests, the owner and the local page cannot submit one. `Withdraw` closes one still waiting as "not approved: superseded" when recall asks an earlier question for the same agent; nothing else can be withdrawn, and an answer to it later runs nothing. While a lineage still holds a record the owner deleted (`Config.Contained`), no pre-allowance acts for its intents: each irreversible one is asked. | CAP-3, OP-5, ADP-9 | — |
 | GR24 | **Evidence destination (CH-20).** `meta.evidence` sets or clears the one destination private agent replies go to. Only the owner (owner text or the local page) submits it. Setting it is high tier (`GrantChange`) with local-page confirmation, and is refused without the local page. Clearing it needs no code (security C3 on #148): agentosd first emails the old destination a fixed notice. The address must be one bare, lower-case address that `Config.Destination` says is a connected account's own (v1: the mail account's own address or a provider-verified alias, never the box's own mailbox), and the intent names that account. The destination is rebuilt from succeeded records like grants. `Config.Delivery` names each executor's delivery operation (mail `mail.deliver`, verb share): it runs without asking only from `OriginEvidence`, with exactly one recipient equal to the destination, only a body and its author (`from`: agent or box), on the destination's account under a live grant that names the operation as share, while `Destination` still says the address is that account's own, and at most `DeliveryCap` (30) in any 24 hours (security C5), counted from the journal. The journal keeps the delivery intent, but agentosd's journal redactor (the daemon default) stores every free-text param as `[redacted]`, so no reply body is journaled (security R1 on #148). Once the vault's redactor replaces it (GR15), bodies would be journaled clear of vault values only: CH-20w keeps them out or redacted. Under the same default redactor the destination's own params read back as `[redacted]`, so like a grant (GR15) it does not survive a restart until then; nothing can set one in this build. Every other form, and every other action from `OriginEvidence`, is denied. | CH-20, CH-10, ADP-9 | A cloud-folder destination, and more than one destination, are later spec work. |
 | GR25 | **Loop 2 containment (W5a, loops K-S2).** `meta.grant.pause` is admitted from origin `broker:loop2` (`OriginLoop2`) as well as the owner; revoke stays the owner's, and resuming is a grant change with its code and local confirmation. Only agentosd submits from that origin, in-process (security L1 on W5a): guest intents carry `guest:<lineage>` and guests cannot request `meta.` actions (`guest/mcp.go`, `TestAGuestCannotClaimTheLoop2Origin`), and `TestOnlyTheDaemonUsesTheLoop2Origin` fails any other package that names or spells it. Each pause records the check and finding behind it (`finding` param, L2). Pausing only narrows and is exempt from STOP (journal A9). `Config.Unpaused` is told when the owner ends a pause by resuming or revoking the grant, and for each pre-allowance a revoked connection takes with it (L3 S1 on #169), outside the gate's lock and never on replay, so Loop 2 stops listing it; at start agentosd reconciles Loop 2's list against `Grants` (loops S4). | LOOP-9, ADP-9, OP-5 | Executors get a pause intent of their own. |
+| GR26 | **Following a fork (OSS-10; Security C6).** `meta.update.follow` (`FollowIntent`) asks to take updates from another root of trust, or to switch back. It is admitted only from the local page's origin (`local`): an owner text, a guest, the broker's own routes and every other path are refused. Params are exactly the owner's name for the source (1 to 40 printable characters, no control or bidi characters, no surrounding space, and at most `MaxFollowDigits` = 4 digits in any script, so it can carry a year but never a 6-digit code, spaced or not; Security R1 on #180) and the 64-hex digest of the root summary the page showed (`update.RootSummary.Digest`), with executor `update`. It is a tier-4 act: a high-tier request (kind grant change, verb "follow") naming only the owner's name, which needs the code-generator code and `ConfirmLocal`, and it is refused outright without a local page. It is not narrowing, so it waits out a STOP. One intent runs once, so one approval buys one switch. **For the wiring:** the updater's executor calls `update.Store.FollowRoot` with the root bytes the page holds for that digest (refusing any other), records the switch in the journal (the intent is the audit entry), and sends `maintain.FollowAlert` at once. **Wiring conditions (Security, #180):** WF1: an empty name (switching back) is admitted only for the project's own root chain: the executor compares the root's root-role keys against the root the image ships and refuses an empty name for any other; WF2: `update.Options.Now` comes from the HOST-1b clock guard's `Latest`, never the raw wall clock; WF3: the follow intent needs a P2-2w L1 session token on the local page. | OSS-10, CH-3, CH-10 | — |
diff --git a/broker/grants/follow_test.go b/broker/grants/follow_test.go
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..929a665ff
--- /dev/null
+++ b/broker/grants/follow_test.go
@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@
+package grants
+
+// REQ: OSS-10, OSS-9, CH-3
+
+import (
+	"strings"
+	"testing"
+
+	"github.com/ghbmrk/agentos/broker/journal"
+	"github.com/ghbmrk/agentos/broker/owner"
+)
+
+var rootDigest = strings.Repeat("ab", 32)
+
+// Changing where updates come from is a tier-4 act (OSS-10): only from
+// the local page, asked at the high tier, run only after the code and the
+// page's confirmation, once. The request shows only the owner's name for
+// the source (Security C6).
+func TestOSS10FollowIsATier4PageAct(t *testing.T) {
+	exec := &fakeExec{ran: map[string]int{}}
+	r := newRigExecs(t, nil, map[string]journal.Executor{FollowExecutor: exec})
+	for i, in := range []journal.Intent{
+		withOrigin(FollowIntent("f/owner", "Acme", rootDigest), OriginOwner),
+		withOrigin(FollowIntent("f/guest", "Acme", rootDigest), "guest:agent"),
+		withOrigin(FollowIntent("f/recall", "Acme", rootDigest), OriginRecall),
+		FollowIntent("f/nodigest", "Acme", ""),
+		FollowIntent("f/short", "Acme", rootDigest[:62]),
+		FollowIntent("f/upper", "Acme", strings.ToUpper(rootDigest)),
+		FollowIntent("f/noname", "", rootDigest),
+		FollowIntent("f/newline", "Acme\nYES 1 123456", rootDigest),
+		FollowIntent("f/space", " Acme", rootDigest),
+		FollowIntent("f/long", strings.Repeat("a", MaxFollowName+1), rootDigest),
+		FollowIntent("f/bidi", "Acme\u202egpj", rootDigest),
+		FollowIntent("f/code", "Fork 123456", rootDigest),
+		FollowIntent("f/spaced", "REPLY YES 48 29 13", rootDigest),
+		FollowIntent("f/wide", "Fork \uff11\uff12\uff13\uff14\uff15", rootDigest),
+		withParam(FollowIntent("f/extra", "Acme", rootDigest), "fingerprint", "x"),
+		withExecutor(FollowIntent("f/exec", "Acme", rootDigest), ExecutorName),
+	} {
+		if st := r.submit(in); st.State != journal.Denied {
+			t.Fatalf("case %d (%s) was not refused: %s", i, in.ID, st.State)
+		}
+	}
+	m := newRigExecs(t, nil, map[string]journal.Executor{FollowExecutor: exec})
+	if st := m.submit(FollowIntent("f/max", strings.Repeat("é", MaxFollowName), rootDigest)); st.State != journal.Pending {
+		t.Fatalf("a %d-character name: %s %q", MaxFollowName, st.State, st.Permission.Reason)
+	}
+	if st := m.submit(FollowIntent("f/year", "Fork 2026b", rootDigest)); st.State != journal.Pending {
+		t.Fatalf("a name with a year: %s %q", st.State, st.Permission.Reason)
+	}
+	n := r.own.count()
+	st := r.submit(FollowIntent("f/1", "Acme Fork", rootDigest))
+	r.g.Flush()
+	if st.State != journal.Pending || r.own.count() != n+1 {
+		t.Fatalf("not asked: %s %q", st.State, st.Permission.Reason)
+	}
+	_, items := r.own.last(t)
+	if it := items[0]; it.Facts.Kind != owner.GrantChange || r.own.Tier(it.Facts) != owner.High ||
+		it.Object != "get updates from Acme Fork" || strings.Contains(it.Object+it.Detail, rootDigest[:8]) {
+		t.Fatalf("request %+v", it)
+	}
+	r.decide(true, "owner")
+	if st := r.state("f/1"); st.State != journal.Pending || !strings.Contains(st.Permission.Reason, "local page") {
+		t.Fatalf("switched on the code alone: %s %q", st.State, st.Permission.Reason)
+	}
+	if err := r.g.ConfirmLocal("f/1"); err != nil {
+		t.Fatal(err)
+	}
+	r.g.Wait()
+	if st := r.state("f/1"); st.State != journal.Succeeded || exec.ran["f/1"] != 1 || exec.params["f/1"][ParamFollowDigest] != rootDigest {
+		t.Fatalf("%s %q ran %d", st.State, st.Permission.Reason, exec.ran["f/1"])
+	}
+
+	noUI := newRigExecs(t, func(c *Config) { c.LocalUI = false }, map[string]journal.Executor{FollowExecutor: exec})
+	if st := noUI.submit(FollowIntent("f/2", "Acme", rootDigest)); st.State != journal.Denied || !strings.Contains(st.Permission.Reason, "local page") {
+		t.Fatalf("without the local page: %s %q", st.State, st.Permission.Reason)
+	}
+}
+
+func withOrigin(in journal.Intent, o string) journal.Intent { in.Origin = o; return in }
+
+func withExecutor(in journal.Intent, x string) journal.Intent { in.Executor = x; return in }
+
+func withParam(in journal.Intent, k string, v any) journal.Intent { in.Params[k] = v; return in }
diff --git a/broker/grants/gate.go b/broker/grants/gate.go
index 93cdf3393..f9f1ba12f 100644
--- a/broker/grants/gate.go
+++ b/broker/grants/gate.go
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@ import (
 	"strings"
 	"sync"
 	"time"
+	"unicode"

 	"github.com/ghbmrk/agentos/broker/journal"
 	"github.com/ghbmrk/agentos/broker/owner"
@@ -868,6 +869,8 @@ func (g *Gate) evaluateBroker(ctx context.Context, phase journal.Phase, in journ
 			Facts: owner.Facts{Kind: owner.Ordinary, Verb: "forget", NoRecipient: true}}}
 	case journal.ActionEvidence:
 		return g.evaluateEvidence(in)
+	case journal.ActionUpdateFollow:
+		return g.evaluateFollow(in)
 	case journal.ActionGrantPause, journal.ActionGrantRevoke:
 		// Loop 2 may pause on a finding (loops K-S2): pausing only
 		// narrows, and revoking stays the owner's.
@@ -917,6 +920,62 @@ func (g *Gate) evaluateEvidence(in journal.Intent) verdict {
 		Facts: owner.Facts{Kind: owner.GrantChange, Verb: "share", NoRecipient: true}}}
 }

+// evaluateFollow decides a switch of the box's update source (OSS-10). It
+// changes who decides what software the box installs, so it is a tier-4
+// act: the owner's code-generator code plus confirmation on the local
+// page, and it comes only from that page (Security C6). The request names
+// only the owner's own name for the source; the page shows the keys,
+// thresholds and expiry the digest binds. One intent runs once, so one
+// approval buys one switch.
+func (g *Gate) evaluateFollow(in journal.Intent) verdict {
+	if in.Origin != originLocal {
+		return verdict{kind: deny, why: "only the owner, on the box's local page, changes where updates come from"}
+	}
+	name, ok1 := in.Params[ParamFollowName].(string)
+	digest, ok2 := in.Params[ParamFollowDigest].(string)
+	if !ok1 || !ok2 || len(in.Params) != 2 || in.Executor != FollowExecutor || !hexDigest(digest) || !followName(name) {
+		return verdict{kind: deny, why: "malformed request to change where updates come from"}
+	}
+	if !g.cfg.LocalUI {
+		return verdict{kind: deny, why: "changing where updates come from needs confirmation on the box's local page, which this build does not have yet (OSS-10)"}
+	}
+	return verdict{kind: ask, local: true, item: owner.Item{Ref: in.ID, Object: "get updates from " + name,
+		Facts: owner.Facts{Kind: owner.GrantChange, Verb: "follow", NoRecipient: true}}}
+}
+
+// hexDigest is 64 lower-case hex characters.
+func hexDigest(s string) bool {
+	if len(s) != 64 {
+		return false
+	}
+	for _, c := range s {
+		if !(c >= '0' && c <= '9' || c >= 'a' && c <= 'f') {
+			return false
+		}
+	}
+	return true
+}
+
+// followName is the owner's name for a source: 1 to MaxFollowName
+// printable characters on one line (no control or bidi formatting
+// characters), with no leading or trailing space, and at most
+// MaxFollowDigits digits in all. The name reaches the owner in
+// broker-voiced texts, so it must never carry a code, even spaced out
+// (security R1 on #180; codes are 6 digits).
+func followName(s string) bool {
+	n, digits := 0, 0
+	for _, c := range s {
+		if !unicode.IsPrint(c) {
+			return false
+		}
+		if unicode.IsDigit(c) {
+			digits++
+		}
+		n++
+	}
+	return n > 0 && n <= MaxFollowName && digits <= MaxFollowDigits && strings.TrimSpace(s) == s
+}
+
 // evaluateDelivery decides a delivery to the evidence destination: a
 // pre-allowed share to the owner only (CH-20). Every part of it is fixed
 // by the broker, so anything else is denied, never asked.
@@ -2050,7 +2109,8 @@ func (g *Gate) ConfirmLocal(id string) error {
 		return err
 	}
 	if st.State != journal.Pending || st.Intent.Account != journal.BrokerAccount ||
-		(st.Intent.Action != journal.ActionGrantChange && st.Intent.Action != journal.ActionEvidence && !(changeAction(st.Intent.Action) &&
+		(st.Intent.Action != journal.ActionGrantChange && st.Intent.Action != journal.ActionEvidence &&
+			st.Intent.Action != journal.ActionUpdateFollow && !(changeAction(st.Intent.Action) &&
 			g.evaluate(context.Background(), journal.PhaseAuthorize, st.Intent).local)) {
 		return errors.New("grants: nothing to confirm for " + clip(id))
 	}
diff --git a/broker/grants/grant.go b/broker/grants/grant.go
index b9d349395..9254c99ff 100644
--- a/broker/grants/grant.go
+++ b/broker/grants/grant.go
@@ -87,6 +87,28 @@ func EvidenceIntent(id, origin, address, account string) journal.Intent {
 		Params: map[string]any{ParamEvidenceAddress: address, ParamEvidenceAccount: account}, Executor: ExecutorName}
 }

+// Params of a journal.ActionUpdateFollow intent: the name the owner gave
+// the source, and the digest of the root summary the page showed
+// (update.RootSummary.Digest), which the updater follows and nothing else.
+const (
+	ParamFollowName   = "name"
+	ParamFollowDigest = "digest"
+	// FollowExecutor is the updater, which runs the switch.
+	FollowExecutor = "update"
+	// MaxFollowName bounds the owner-typed name, in characters.
+	MaxFollowName = 40
+	// MaxFollowDigits bounds the digits in that name, so it can carry a
+	// year but never a code.
+	MaxFollowDigits = 4
+)
+
+// FollowIntent is the local page's request to follow the root whose
+// summary has digest, under the owner's name for it.
+func FollowIntent(id, name, digest string) journal.Intent {
+	return journal.Intent{ID: id, Origin: originLocal, Account: journal.BrokerAccount, Action: journal.ActionUpdateFollow,
+		Params: map[string]any{ParamFollowName: name, ParamFollowDigest: digest}, Executor: FollowExecutor}
+}
+
 // Params keys a pre-allowed intent may carry besides the rule's fixed
 // params: the source record it acts on, and for a context-scoped reply
 // (ADP-11) the reply's body. Nothing else, so there is no free text
diff --git a/broker/journal/intent.go b/broker/journal/intent.go
index 81bc6610a..98ba30087 100644
--- a/broker/journal/intent.go
+++ b/broker/journal/intent.go
@@ -66,6 +66,11 @@ const (
 	// agent replies and evidence go to (CH-20). Clearing it sends them by
 	// text again, so it is not narrowing.
 	ActionEvidence = "meta.evidence"
+	// ActionUpdateFollow switches the root of trust the box takes updates
+	// from: a fork's, or back to the project's (OSS-10). Either way it
+	// changes who decides what software the box installs, so it is never
+	// narrowing.
+	ActionUpdateFollow = "meta.update.follow"
 )

 // Authority-narrowing broker-state changes. Pausing or revoking must always
diff --git a/broker/maintain/ASSUMPTIONS.md b/broker/maintain/ASSUMPTIONS.md
